---
title: "Overlays"
---

Overlays are used for displaying messages over the top of the grid.
There are a number of provided overlays triggered by grid state and support for custom overlays controlled by the application.

## Grid Provided Overlays

The grid provides the following built-in overlays that will be shown automatically based on grid state unless disabled:
- Loading overlay - shown when data is loading
- No rows overlay - shown when there are no rows to display
- No matching filter overlay - shown when no rows match the current filter
- Excel export overlay - shown when data is being exported to Excel

{% gridExampleRunner title="Loading overlay" name="loading-overlay"  exampleHeight=350 /%}

## Custom Overlays

Applications can provide their own custom overlays and control when they are displayed. This enables full control over the content and timing of overlays shown in the grid.

This is configured via the `activeOverlay` and `activeOverlayParams` grid options.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Active Overlay Switcher" name="active-overlay-switcher" exampleHeight=350 /%}